Article 17

(1) The Regent conducts development of PPT development. (2) Development as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. provision of implementation guidelines;

b. guidance;

c. supervision;

d. monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of services for women and child victims of violence, for both apparatus and the community.

Article 19

(1) In providing protection for women and child victims of violence, the community may:

a. establish family partners at the sub-district/village level in coordination with Desa Pakraman;
b. establish women and child protection units within community organizations;
c. conduct socialization of women and children's rights independently;
d. provide first aid to victims; and e. report to the competent authorities if violence against victims occurs in their environment.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by individuals, Desa Pakraman, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, the private sector, and mass media.

Article 4

The rights of victims include:

a. protection from the family;
b. protection from the police;
c. protection from the prosecutor's office;
d. protection from the court;
e. protection from advocates,
f. protection from social institutions, or other parties either temporarily or based on the stipulation of a protection order from the court;
g. health services according to medical needs; h. special handling related to victim confidentiality;
i. accompaniment by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
j. spiritual guidance services; and
k. victims have the right to determine their own decisions regarding which options will be implemented.

Article 7

(1) PPT services include:

a. providing services and handling as quickly as possible to victims;
b. providing convenience, comfort, safety, and free of charge for victims;
c. maintaining the confidentiality of victims; and
d. guaranteeing justice and legal certainty for victims. (2) The procedure for PPT services as referred to in paragraph (1) is regulated by Regent Regulation;

